When only `branchChangeIcon` exists (no `branchTestIcon`), the layout renders `[<StatusSlotPlaceholder />] [change button]` — the change icon ends up in the RIGHT (test) slot position. The first ternary `branchChangeIcon && branchTestIcon` is `false`, so it renders a placeholder in the left slot; the second ternary `branchTestIcon` is also `false`, so the change button falls into the `else` branch and occupies the right slot. This is semantically inconsistent: when both icons exist, change is on the left; when only change exists, it shifts to the right. Consider simplifying to two independent slot renders with per-slot placeholders:
```tsx
{branchChangeIcon ? (
  <StatusButton ariaLabel={`Change status: ...`} ...>{branchChangeIcon}</StatusButton>
) : (
  <StatusSlotPlaceholder aria-hidden="true" />
)}
{branchTestIcon ? (
  <StatusButton ariaLabel={`Test status: ...`} ...>{branchTestIcon}</StatusButton>
) : (
  <StatusSlotPlaceholder aria-hidden="true" />
)}
```
This keeps change consistently in the left slot and test in the right.
